Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Load pretrained map modules and add map-channel ablation
 flags

Pretraining stores the fusion under bert.global_encoder.graph_map_attention
and the map encoder as map_encoder.*; the navigation model owns the fusion
at the top level and never loaded the map encoder, so HF dropped all 43
tensors as unused in every DAgger run. Remap the fusion keys, load the map
encoder strictly, verify the transfer, and gate it behind
MODEL.MAP_ENCODER.load_pretrained_map_modules (True by default).

Also add MODEL.MAP_ENCODER.map_ablation (none, metadata_only, raster_only,
no_direction) and MODEL.MAP_ENCODER.start_position_scale for eval-time
channel attribution, and let eval_s4.sh take PRETRAINED_CKPT and
LOAD_PRETRAINED_MAP_MODULES from the environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
